{
  "_comment": [
    "Maps each app resource-type id to an exact filename inside the official AWS",
    "Architecture Icons asset package (https://aws.amazon.com/architecture/icons/).",
    "",
    "Matching is by EXACT basename, never substring: 'Arch_Amazon-EC2_64.svg' and",
    "'Arch_Amazon-EC2-Auto-Scaling_64.svg' are different icons, as are",
    "'Arch_Amazon-Simple-Storage-Service_64.svg' and the Glacier variant.",
    "",
    "Service icons live in Architecture-Service-Icons_*/ at 64px. NAT Gateway is a",
    "resource icon, not a service icon, so it comes from Resource-Icons_*/ at 48px.",
    "",
    "The key set here must exactly match the AWS_ICONS keys in server-v1.js;",
    "sync-aws-icons.js enforces that and fails on drift.",
    "",
    "'generic' is the fallback icon shown for any resource type without a",
    "specific mapping, so the UI never falls back to a bare text badge."
  ],
  "icons": {
    "ec2": "Arch_Amazon-EC2_64.svg",
    "asg": "Arch_Amazon-EC2-Auto-Scaling_64.svg",
    "lambda": "Arch_AWS-Lambda_64.svg",
